  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Humanitarian Assistance to Mauritanian Returnees, Migrants, and Host Communities in Hodh Chargui (Mauritania)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Despite internal security and political stability, Mauritania is directly affected by regional volatility. Since 2012, violence in Mali has led to an influx of refugees into the Mberra camp in the Hodh Chargui region, which housed 67,466 refugees as of October 2021. Since the beginning of 2022, heightened tensions and multiplication of incidents have been observed, despite the efforts made by both countries to investigate the situation and maintain peaceful coexistence between the communities. This project&#x2019;s overall objective is to provide urgent humanitarian assistance to returnees and migrants in the border area of Hodh Chargui. The project focuses on two main components: i) improving urgent access to water to returnees and migrants in the border area of Hodh Chargui; ii) providing emergency livelihood support.</narrative>
  </description>
